{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c497","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b9e-4019-7d82-8599-f430d1ae00b2"},"sequence":166,"recorded_at":1780531400000327,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"badde784-d98e-401b-9c95-32d1221bf072"},"task_id":"badde784-d98e-401b-9c95-32d1221bf072","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"badde784-d98e-401b-9c95-32d1221bf072","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1454 line(s) above)\n1455|### 5.1 Session Record\n1456|\n1457|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1458|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1459|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1460|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1461|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1462|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1463|\n1464|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1465|| --- | --- | --- |\n1466|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1467|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1468|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1469|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1470|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Globally unique |\n1471|| <code>name</code> | string | Section 2.3 grammar |\n1472|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>direct</code> or <code>task_board</code> |\n1473|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic time |\n1474|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Allowlisted host at creation |\n1475|| <code>provider_id</code> | string | Lowercase plugin ID |\n1476|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Required |\n1477|| <code>execution_profile</code> | enum | <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code> |\n1478|| <code>launch_plan</code> | Launch Plan | Closed shape below; sanitized and secret-free |\n1479|| <code>task_board</code> | Task-board Reference or null | Required object exactly when <code>kind = task_board</code> |\n1480|| <code>fork_provenance</code> | Fork Provenance or null | Required object exactly when this record was created by fork |\n1481|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Required; may be empty; reverse-DNS keys only |\n1482|\n1483|The embedded Launch Plan is a closed object with exactly these members:\n1484|\n1485|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1486|| --- | --- | --- |\n1487|| <code>argv</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[1..128] | Each element is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes; total encoded argv is at most 65,536 bytes; never a shell command string |\n1488|| <code>cwd_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Names one workspace in the Session Record's workspace group |\n1489|| <code>cwd_relative</code> | string | <code>.</code> for the workspace root or a path satisfying Section 1.6 |\n1490|| <code>env_names</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[0..64] | Sorted, unique names matching <code>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}</code>; values resolve only from destination-local state |\n1491|| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\n1492|| <code>contains_secrets</code> | boolean | MUST be false |\n1493|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1494|\n1495|Arguments MUST contain only sanitized provider/task-board arguments. Secret\n1496|values, inline credential-bearing URLs, response files containing secrets, and\n1497|shell fragments are forbidden. A name such as <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> in\n1498|<code>env_names</code> is a destination-local lookup instruction, not a stored\n1499|value.\n1500|\n1501|The Task-board Reference is a closed object:\n1502|\n1503|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1504|| --- | --- | --- |\n1505|| <code>bridge_protocol_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1506|| <code>board</code> | Board Identity | Closed shape below |\n1507|| <code>task_element_id</code> | string | 1–128 printable non-control UTF-8 bytes |\n1508|| <code>launch_mode</code> | enum | <code>primary_owner</code> or <code>tracked_prompt</code> |\n1509|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string or null | MUST be null in the immutable creation record; the public reference is established by <code>task_board.launched</code> and may later change through <code>task_board.adopted</code> |\n1510|| <code>board_goal</code> | Board Goal or null | Required non-null for <code>primary_owner</code> |\n1511|| <code>native_goal_binding</code> | enum | <code>bound</code>, <code>prompt</code>, or <code>none</code> |\n1512|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1513|\n1514|Board Identity has exactly <code>kind</code> (<code>local</code> or\n1515|<code>remote</code>), <code>logical_id</code> (1–128 characters matching\n1516|<code>[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}</code>),\n1517|<code>remote_url</code> (absolute <code>https</code> URL or null), and\n1518|<code>extensions</code>. A local board requires null <code>remote_url</code>;\n1519|a remote board requires a URL with no userinfo, query, or fragment. Board Goal\n1520|has exactly <code>schema = \"board-goal-v2\"</code>, <code>goal_id</code> as a\n1521|1–128 character public goal reference, <code>revision</code> as uint53 greater\n1522|than zero, and <code>extensions</code>. <code>primary_owner</code> requires\n1523|<code>native_goal_binding = bound</code>; <code>tracked_prompt</code> permits\n1524|<code>prompt</code> or <code>none</code> and MAY have a null goal.\n1525|\n1526|The creation-time <code>manager_session_ref</code> MUST be null for both launch\n1527|modes. This avoids making an immutable Session Record depend on a manager\n1528|reference that the public bridge has not created yet. The current reference is\n1529|the newest authoritative <code>task_board.launched</code> or\n1530|<code>task_board.adopted</code> event for the session; a missing event means the\n1531|task-board launch has not succeeded and MUST NOT be guessed from private state.\n1532|\n1533|Fork Provenance is a closed object with exactly\n1534|<code>source_session_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> digest,\n1535|<code>source_workspace_group_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>operation_id</code>\n1536|UUIDv7, <code>provider_fork_mode</code> as <code>native</code>,\n1537|<code>supported_import</code>, or <code>task_board_clone</code>, and\n1538|<code>extensions</code>. It is core provenance, not an extension, and MUST\n1539|remain immutable with the fork's Session Record.\n1540|\n1541|Normative example:\n1542|\n1543|~~~json\n1544|{\n1545|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1546|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1547|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:d61701066a7f5dd37bf35fea0e85e7f154251355ad24a49976532d7f79ddc772\",\n1548|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1549|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1550|  \"name\": \"payments-api\",\n1551|  \"kind\": \"direct\",\n1552|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:00:00.000Z\",\n1553|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1554|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n1555|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n1556|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n1557|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1558|    \"argv\": [\"codex\"],\n1559|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n1560|    \"cwd_relative\": \"src\",\n1561|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n1562|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1563|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1564|    \"extensions\": {}\n1565|  },\n1566|  \"task_board\": null,\n1567|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1568|  \"extensions\": {}\n1569|}\n1570|~~~\n1571|\n1572|A task-board Session Record uses the same Launch Plan shape and this exact\n1573|tagged variant:\n1574|\n1575|~~~json\n1576|{\n1577|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1578|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1579|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:0acd3e31635372e176f8f37b1b74aa0ebdcf2d1e4ac40d43adb8e462079b34a2\",\n1580|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1581|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1582|  \"name\": \"qwen-investigation\",\n1583|  \"kind\": \"task_board\",\n1584|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:01:00.000Z\",\n1585|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1586|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n1587|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-af70-7188-8172-1234567890ab\",\n1588|  \"execution_profile\": \"standard\",\n1589|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1590|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n1591|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n1592|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n1593|    \"env_names\": [],\n1594|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1595|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1596|    \"extensions\": {}\n1597|  },\n1598|  \"task_board\": {\n1599|    \"bridge_protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1600|    \"board\": {\n1601|      \"kind\": \"local\",\n1602|      \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n1603|      \"remote_url\": null,\n1604|      \"extensions\": {}\n1605|    },\n1606|    \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n1607|    \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n1608|    \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n1609|    \"board_goal\": null,\n1610|    \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\",\n1611|    \"extensions\": {}\n1612|  },\n1613|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1614|  \"extensions\": {}\n1615|}\n1616|~~~\n1617|\n1618|The example <code>record_id</code>, like every self-identity digest in this\n1619|document, is the computed canonical digest. Validators MUST recompute it and\n1620|MUST reject a mismatch.\n1621|\n1622|Session Record 2.0.0 is emitted in v0.3.0 only for a cross-environment clone\n1623|target. It retains every major-1 field except <code>fork_provenance</code>,\n1624|which is replaced by required closed <code>derivation_provenance</code>.\n1625|Provider Protocol 2 launch/fork continues to emit and consume Session Record\n1626|1.0.0 with its exact nullable fork provenance; no in-place migration or silent\n1627|major retry is permitted.\n1628|\n1629|The derivation union has tags <code>origin</code>,\n1630|<code>same_provider_fork</code>, and <code>cross_environment_clone</code>.\n1631|The first two are reserved/read-only in v0.3 until a containing Provider\n1632|protocol adopts them. Cross-environment clone contains exactly:\n1633|\n1634|- <code>kind=cross_environment_clone</code>, operation UUIDv7, and bundle UUIDv7;\n1635|- <code>source_kind=ax_session|external_native</code>;\n1636|- nullable source Session Record, Checkpoint, and Provider Identity IDs, all\n1637|  non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>;\n1638|- a sanitized non-authoritative source native session ID;\n1639|- exact source and target Environment Tuples;\n1640|- source snapshot, Capture Manifest, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, and\n1641|  Migration Checkpoint digests;\n1642|- nullable previous Lineage Receipt and source profile Event IDs; and\n1643|- reverse-DNS extensions.\n1644|\n1645|The reserved <code>origin</code> variant contains exactly\n1646|<code>kind=origin</code>, <code>creation_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n1647|<code>extensions</code>. The reserved <code>same_provider_fork</code> variant\n1648|contains exactly <code>kind=same_provider_fork</code>,\n1649|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1650|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1651|<code>source_workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1652|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1653|<code>provider_fork_mode:native|supported_import|task_board_clone</code>,\n1654|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1655|\n1656|The <code>cross_environment_clone</code> variant's exact typed members are\n1657|<code>kind</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1658|<code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1659|<code>source_kind:ax_session|external_native</code>,\n1660|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n1661|<code>source_session_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1662|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n1663|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1664|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n1665|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1666|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1667|<code>source_snapshot_digest:digest</code>,\n1668|<code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n1669|<code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>,\n1670|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n1671|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1672|<code>previous_lineage_receipt_id:digest|null</code>,\n1673|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1674|All four AX-source IDs are non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>.\n1675|\n1676|The new target Session ID and target <code>provider_id</code> are allocated at\n1677|creation and never reuse or mutate the source Session or source provider ID.\n1678|Target native identity, final reports, target Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt\n1679|are absent because they do not exist yet; Provider Identity and immutable clone\n1680|events bind those later facts without mutating the record or forming a digest\n1681|cycle. Task-board references remain orthogonal authority in the existing\n1682|<code>task_board</code> field; source goals, manager references, leases,\n1683|approvals, tokens, and pending operations do not transfer.\n1684|\n1685|Session Record 3.0.0 is the v0.4 creation contract. It retains every v2\n1686|top-level member and replaces the v2 derivation union with the closed creation\n1687|union <code>origin</code>, <code>same_provider_fork</code>,\n1688|<code>cross_environment_clone</code>, and <code>native_adoption</code>. The\n1689|first three retain their v2 exact shapes and semantics. The new\n1690|<code>native_adoption</code> variant contains exactly\n1691|<code>kind=native_adoption</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1692|<code>source_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_instance_id:digest</code>,\n1693|<code>source_observation_id:digest</code>,\n1694|<code>source_head_digest:digest</code>,\n1695|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1696|<code>target_provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n1697|and <code>extensions</code>. These are creation inputs only. Provider Identity,\n1698|first Checkpoint, adoption events, and Directory Operation Receipts are later\n1699|facts and MUST NOT appear in the creation record.\n1700|\n1701|Adoption creates a new Session ID around the existing native identity and does\n1702|not claim that pre-adoption history was AX-authored or fenced. Provider ID is\n1703|immutable after creation. Cross-environment move uses the existing\n1704|<code>cross_environment_clone</code> creation variant plus later Session Event\n1705|3/Directory Operation Receipt move lifecycle; it is not a fifth creation tag\n1706|and never rewrites the source Session.\n1707|\n1708|Session Record 1 and 2 remain readable and immutable. New origin/fork/clone/\n1709|adopt records written by a directory-capable v0.4 implementation use major 3;\n1710|no reader silently retries another major or translates an existing record in\n1711|place.\n1712|\n1713|### 5.2 Session Event\n1714|\n1715|This subsection defines the immutable Session Event <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1716|variant used for post-creation changes under Session Record 1. It uses schema\n1717|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-event</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1718|13.14.5 and 13.15 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1719|<code>3.0.0</code> event variants; a reader MUST select the exact registered\n1720|major and MUST NOT interpret this base definition as their complete schema.\n1721|\n1722|Required fields are <code>event_id</code> digest, <code>subject_id</code> and\n1723|<code>session_id</code> with the same UUID,\n1724|<code>event_type</code>, <code>created_by_host_id</code>,\n1725|<code>lease_epoch</code>, <code>lease_id</code>, and\n1726|<code>lease_sequence</code> as a uint53 starting at 1 for\n1727|each lease,\n1728|<code>predecessors</code> as a sorted array of one or more record/event digests,\n1729|<code>created_at</code>, and <code>payload</code>. The first event after\n1730|creation MUST have exactly the Session Record ID in\n1731|<code>predecessors</code>; later events reference one or more prior event heads.\n1732|Events form a DAG; they are not ordered by timestamp.\n1733|The exact top-level shape also requires <code>schema</code>,\n1734|<code>schema_version</code>, and <code>extensions</code>; no other top-level\n1735|member is permitted.\n1736|\n1737|The winning owner MUST serialize state-changing events for a session. Within\n1738|one lease, <code>lease_sequence</code> MUST increase by exactly one and each\n1739|event MUST reference the immediately prior authoritative event. The first event\n1740|under a successor lease uses sequence 1 and references the predecessor\n1741|checkpoint's authoritative event heads. A missing sequence, two different\n1742|events at one sequence under the winning lease, or an event that omits the\n1743|required predecessor is <code>invalid_state_transition</code>; the session MUST\n1744|park and MUST NOT accept input until a newer explicit takeover establishes an\n1745|unambiguous checkpoint. Losing-lease branches remain preserved but are never\n1746|applied to authoritative state.\n1747|\n1748|The v1 event types are:\n1749|\n1750|<code>session.created</code>, <code>terminal.created</code>,\n1751|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>provider.identified</code>,\n1752|<code>session.idle</code>, <code>session.quiescing</code>,\n1753|<code>checkpoint.created</code>, <code>sync.completed</code>,\n1754|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1755|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1756|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1757|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1758|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1759|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1760|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1761|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1762|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1763|\n1764|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1765|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1766|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1767|\n1768|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1769|| --- | --- |\n1770|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1771|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1772|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1773|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1774|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1775|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1776|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1777|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1778|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1779|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1780|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1781|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1782|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1783|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1784|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1785|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1786|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1787|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1788|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1789|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1790|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1791|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1792|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1793|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1794|\n1795|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1796|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1797|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1798|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1799|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1800|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1801|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1802|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1803|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1804|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1805|null.\n1806|\n1807|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1808|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1809|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1810|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1811|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1812|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1813|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1814|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1815|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1816|\n1817|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1818|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1819|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1820|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1821|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1822|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1823|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1824|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1825|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1826|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1827|\n1828|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1829|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1830|\n1831|Normative example:\n1832|\n1833|~~~json\n1834|{\n1835|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1836|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1837|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1838|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1839|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1840|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1841|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1842|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1843|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1844|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1845|  \"predecessors\": [\n1846|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1847|  ],\n1848|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1849|  \"payload\": {\n1850|    \"graceful\": true,\n1851|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1852|    \"resumable\": true,\n1853|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1854|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1855|    \"store_closed\": true\n1856|  },\n1857|  \"extensions\": {}\n1858|}\n1859|~~~\n1860|\n1861|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1862|\n1863|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1864|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1865|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1866|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1867|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1868|\n1869|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1870|| --- | --- |\n1871|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1872|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1873|\n1874|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1875|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1876|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1877|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1878|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1879|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1880|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1881|\n1882|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1883|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1884|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1885|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1886|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1887|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1888|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1889|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1890|version replacement.\n1891|\n1892|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1893|\n1894|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1895|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1896|\n1897|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1898|| --- | --- | --- |\n1899|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1900|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1901|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1902|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1903|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1904|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n1905|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n1906|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n1907|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n1908|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n1909|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n1910|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n1911|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n1912|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1913|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1914|\n1915|The object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\n1916|Normative example:\n1917|\n1918|~~~json\n1919|{\n1920|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:lease\",\n1921|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1922|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:8ead987abed8c7c05175b447c9a0e2b3a521f12e5a989acb8abe132576852d63\",\n1923|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1924|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1925|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1926|  \"epoch\": 4,\n1927|  \"holder_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1928|  \"predecessor_lease_id\": \"bbbbbbbb-cccc-4ddd-8eee-ffffffffffff\",\n1929|  \"reason\": \"graceful_takeover\",\n1930|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1931|  \"issued_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1932|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1933|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:00.000Z\",\n1934|  \"extensions\": {}\n1935|}\n1936|~~~\n1937|\n1938|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n1939|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n1940|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n1941|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n1942|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n1943|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n1944|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n1945|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n1946|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n1947|\n1948|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n1949|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n1950|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n1951|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n1952|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n1953|\n1954|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c499","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b9e-4019-7d82-8599-f430d1ae00b2"},"sequence":167,"recorded_at":1780531400000329,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"badde784-d98e-401b-9c95-32d1221bf072"},"task_id":"badde784-d98e-401b-9c95-32d1221bf072","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"badde784-d98e-401b-9c95-32d1221bf072"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c49b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b9e-4019-7d82-8599-f430d1ae00b2"},"sequence":168,"recorded_at":1780531400000331,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887"},"call_id":"call_01a07b9eacce7531b160dbdee3307d6d","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1454 line(s) above)\n1455|### 5.1 Session Record\n1456|\n1457|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1458|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1459|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1460|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1461|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1462|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1463|\n1464|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1465|| --- | --- | --- |\n1466|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1467|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1468|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1469|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1470|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Globally unique |\n1471|| <code>name</code> | string | Section 2.3 grammar |\n1472|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>direct</code> or <code>task_board</code> |\n1473|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic time |\n1474|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Allowlisted host at creation |\n1475|| <code>provider_id</code> | string | Lowercase plugin ID |\n1476|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Required |\n1477|| <code>execution_profile</code> | enum | <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code> |\n1478|| <code>launch_plan</code> | Launch Plan | Closed shape below; sanitized and secret-free |\n1479|| <code>task_board</code> | Task-board Reference or null | Required object exactly when <code>kind = task_board</code> |\n1480|| <code>fork_provenance</code> | Fork Provenance or null | Required object exactly when this record was created by fork |\n1481|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Required; may be empty; reverse-DNS keys only |\n1482|\n1483|The embedded Launch Plan is a closed object with exactly these members:\n1484|\n1485|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1486|| --- | --- | --- |\n1487|| <code>argv</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[1..128] | Each element is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes; total encoded argv is at most 65,536 bytes; never a shell command string |\n1488|| <code>cwd_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Names one workspace in the Session Record's workspace group |\n1489|| <code>cwd_relative</code> | string | <code>.</code> for the workspace root or a path satisfying Section 1.6 |\n1490|| <code>env_names</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[0..64] | Sorted, unique names matching <code>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}</code>; values resolve only from destination-local state |\n1491|| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\n1492|| <code>contains_secrets</code> | boolean | MUST be false |\n1493|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1494|\n1495|Arguments MUST contain only sanitized provider/task-board arguments. Secret\n1496|values, inline credential-bearing URLs, response files containing secrets, and\n1497|shell fragments are forbidden. A name such as <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> in\n1498|<code>env_names</code> is a destination-local lookup instruction, not a stored\n1499|value.\n1500|\n1501|The Task-board Reference is a closed object:\n1502|\n1503|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1504|| --- | --- | --- |\n1505|| <code>bridge_protocol_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1506|| <code>board</code> | Board Identity | Closed shape below |\n1507|| <code>task_element_id</code> | string | 1–128 printable non-control UTF-8 bytes |\n1508|| <code>launch_mode</code> | enum | <code>primary_owner</code> or <code>tracked_prompt</code> |\n1509|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string or null | MUST be null in the immutable creation record; the public reference is established by <code>task_board.launched</code> and may later change through <code>task_board.adopted</code> |\n1510|| <code>board_goal</code> | Board Goal or null | Required non-null for <code>primary_owner</code> |\n1511|| <code>native_goal_binding</code> | enum | <code>bound</code>, <code>prompt</code>, or <code>none</code> |\n1512|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1513|\n1514|Board Identity has exactly <code>kind</code> (<code>local</code> or\n1515|<code>remote</code>), <code>logical_id</code> (1–128 characters matching\n1516|<code>[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}</code>),\n1517|<code>remote_url</code> (absolute <code>https</code> URL or null), and\n1518|<code>extensions</code>. A local board requires null <code>remote_url</code>;\n1519|a remote board requires a URL with no userinfo, query, or fragment. Board Goal\n1520|has exactly <code>schema = \"board-goal-v2\"</code>, <code>goal_id</code> as a\n1521|1–128 character public goal reference, <code>revision</code> as uint53 greater\n1522|than zero, and <code>extensions</code>. <code>primary_owner</code> requires\n1523|<code>native_goal_binding = bound</code>; <code>tracked_prompt</code> permits\n1524|<code>prompt</code> or <code>none</code> and MAY have a null goal.\n1525|\n1526|The creation-time <code>manager_session_ref</code> MUST be null for both launch\n1527|modes. This avoids making an immutable Session Record depend on a manager\n1528|reference that the public bridge has not created yet. The current reference is\n1529|the newest authoritative <code>task_board.launched</code> or\n1530|<code>task_board.adopted</code> event for the session; a missing event means the\n1531|task-board launch has not succeeded and MUST NOT be guessed from private state.\n1532|\n1533|Fork Provenance is a closed object with exactly\n1534|<code>source_session_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> digest,\n1535|<code>source_workspace_group_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>operation_id</code>\n1536|UUIDv7, <code>provider_fork_mode</code> as <code>native</code>,\n1537|<code>supported_import</code>, or <code>task_board_clone</code>, and\n1538|<code>extensions</code>. It is core provenance, not an extension, and MUST\n1539|remain immutable with the fork's Session Record.\n1540|\n1541|Normative example:\n1542|\n1543|~~~json\n1544|{\n1545|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1546|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1547|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:d61701066a7f5dd37bf35fea0e85e7f154251355ad24a49976532d7f79ddc772\",\n1548|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1549|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1550|  \"name\": \"payments-api\",\n1551|  \"kind\": \"direct\",\n1552|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:00:00.000Z\",\n1553|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1554|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n1555|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n1556|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n1557|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1558|    \"argv\": [\"codex\"],\n1559|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n1560|    \"cwd_relative\": \"src\",\n1561|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n1562|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1563|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1564|    \"extensions\": {}\n1565|  },\n1566|  \"task_board\": null,\n1567|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1568|  \"extensions\": {}\n1569|}\n1570|~~~\n1571|\n1572|A task-board Session Record uses the same Launch Plan shape and this exact\n1573|tagged variant:\n1574|\n1575|~~~json\n1576|{\n1577|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1578|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1579|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:0acd3e31635372e176f8f37b1b74aa0ebdcf2d1e4ac40d43adb8e462079b34a2\",\n1580|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1581|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1582|  \"name\": \"qwen-investigation\",\n1583|  \"kind\": \"task_board\",\n1584|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:01:00.000Z\",\n1585|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1586|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n1587|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-af70-7188-8172-1234567890ab\",\n1588|  \"execution_profile\": \"standard\",\n1589|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1590|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n1591|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n1592|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n1593|    \"env_names\": [],\n1594|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1595|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1596|    \"extensions\": {}\n1597|  },\n1598|  \"task_board\": {\n1599|    \"bridge_protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1600|    \"board\": {\n1601|      \"kind\": \"local\",\n1602|      \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n1603|      \"remote_url\": null,\n1604|      \"extensions\": {}\n1605|    },\n1606|    \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n1607|    \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n1608|    \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n1609|    \"board_goal\": null,\n1610|    \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\",\n1611|    \"extensions\": {}\n1612|  },\n1613|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1614|  \"extensions\": {}\n1615|}\n1616|~~~\n1617|\n1618|The example <code>record_id</code>, like every self-identity digest in this\n1619|document, is the computed canonical digest. Validators MUST recompute it and\n1620|MUST reject a mismatch.\n1621|\n1622|Session Record 2.0.0 is emitted in v0.3.0 only for a cross-environment clone\n1623|target. It retains every major-1 field except <code>fork_provenance</code>,\n1624|which is replaced by required closed <code>derivation_provenance</code>.\n1625|Provider Protocol 2 launch/fork continues to emit and consume Session Record\n1626|1.0.0 with its exact nullable fork provenance; no in-place migration or silent\n1627|major retry is permitted.\n1628|\n1629|The derivation union has tags <code>origin</code>,\n1630|<code>same_provider_fork</code>, and <code>cross_environment_clone</code>.\n1631|The first two are reserved/read-only in v0.3 until a containing Provider\n1632|protocol adopts them. Cross-environment clone contains exactly:\n1633|\n1634|- <code>kind=cross_environment_clone</code>, operation UUIDv7, and bundle UUIDv7;\n1635|- <code>source_kind=ax_session|external_native</code>;\n1636|- nullable source Session Record, Checkpoint, and Provider Identity IDs, all\n1637|  non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>;\n1638|- a sanitized non-authoritative source native session ID;\n1639|- exact source and target Environment Tuples;\n1640|- source snapshot, Capture Manifest, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, and\n1641|  Migration Checkpoint digests;\n1642|- nullable previous Lineage Receipt and source profile Event IDs; and\n1643|- reverse-DNS extensions.\n1644|\n1645|The reserved <code>origin</code> variant contains exactly\n1646|<code>kind=origin</code>, <code>creation_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n1647|<code>extensions</code>. The reserved <code>same_provider_fork</code> variant\n1648|contains exactly <code>kind=same_provider_fork</code>,\n1649|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1650|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1651|<code>source_workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1652|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1653|<code>provider_fork_mode:native|supported_import|task_board_clone</code>,\n1654|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1655|\n1656|The <code>cross_environment_clone</code> variant's exact typed members are\n1657|<code>kind</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1658|<code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1659|<code>source_kind:ax_session|external_native</code>,\n1660|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n1661|<code>source_session_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1662|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n1663|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1664|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n1665|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1666|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1667|<code>source_snapshot_digest:digest</code>,\n1668|<code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n1669|<code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>,\n1670|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n1671|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1672|<code>previous_lineage_receipt_id:digest|null</code>,\n1673|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1674|All four AX-source IDs are non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>.\n1675|\n1676|The new target Session ID and target <code>provider_id</code> are allocated at\n1677|creation and never reuse or mutate the source Session or source provider ID.\n1678|Target native identity, final reports, target Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt\n1679|are absent because they do not exist yet; Provider Identity and immutable clone\n1680|events bind those later facts without mutating the record or forming a digest\n1681|cycle. Task-board references remain orthogonal authority in the existing\n1682|<code>task_board</code> field; source goals, manager references, leases,\n1683|approvals, tokens, and pending operations do not transfer.\n1684|\n1685|Session Record 3.0.0 is the v0.4 creation contract. It retains every v2\n1686|top-level member and replaces the v2 derivation union with the closed creation\n1687|union <code>origin</code>, <code>same_provider_fork</code>,\n1688|<code>cross_environment_clone</code>, and <code>native_adoption</code>. The\n1689|first three retain their v2 exact shapes and semantics. The new\n1690|<code>native_adoption</code> variant contains exactly\n1691|<code>kind=native_adoption</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1692|<code>source_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_instance_id:digest</code>,\n1693|<code>source_observation_id:digest</code>,\n1694|<code>source_head_digest:digest</code>,\n1695|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1696|<code>target_provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n1697|and <code>extensions</code>. These are creation inputs only. Provider Identity,\n1698|first Checkpoint, adoption events, and Directory Operation Receipts are later\n1699|facts and MUST NOT appear in the creation record.\n1700|\n1701|Adoption creates a new Session ID around the existing native identity and does\n1702|not claim that pre-adoption history was AX-authored or fenced. Provider ID is\n1703|immutable after creation. Cross-environment move uses the existing\n1704|<code>cross_environment_clone</code> creation variant plus later Session Event\n1705|3/Directory Operation Receipt move lifecycle; it is not a fifth creation tag\n1706|and never rewrites the source Session.\n1707|\n1708|Session Record 1 and 2 remain readable and immutable. New origin/fork/clone/\n1709|adopt records written by a directory-capable v0.4 implementation use major 3;\n1710|no reader silently retries another major or translates an existing record in\n1711|place.\n1712|\n1713|### 5.2 Session Event\n1714|\n1715|This subsection defines the immutable Session Event <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1716|variant used for post-creation changes under Session Record 1. It uses schema\n1717|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-event</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1718|13.14.5 and 13.15 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1719|<code>3.0.0</code> event variants; a reader MUST select the exact registered\n1720|major and MUST NOT interpret this base definition as their complete schema.\n1721|\n1722|Required fields are <code>event_id</code> digest, <code>subject_id</code> and\n1723|<code>session_id</code> with the same UUID,\n1724|<code>event_type</code>, <code>created_by_host_id</code>,\n1725|<code>lease_epoch</code>, <code>lease_id</code>, and\n1726|<code>lease_sequence</code> as a uint53 starting at 1 for\n1727|each lease,\n1728|<code>predecessors</code> as a sorted array of one or more record/event digests,\n1729|<code>created_at</code>, and <code>payload</code>. The first event after\n1730|creation MUST have exactly the Session Record ID in\n1731|<code>predecessors</code>; later events reference one or more prior event heads.\n1732|Events form a DAG; they are not ordered by timestamp.\n1733|The exact top-level shape also requires <code>schema</code>,\n1734|<code>schema_version</code>, and <code>extensions</code>; no other top-level\n1735|member is permitted.\n1736|\n1737|The winning owner MUST serialize state-changing events for a session. Within\n1738|one lease, <code>lease_sequence</code> MUST increase by exactly one and each\n1739|event MUST reference the immediately prior authoritative event. The first event\n1740|under a successor lease uses sequence 1 and references the predecessor\n1741|checkpoint's authoritative event heads. A missing sequence, two different\n1742|events at one sequence under the winning lease, or an event that omits the\n1743|required predecessor is <code>invalid_state_transition</code>; the session MUST\n1744|park and MUST NOT accept input until a newer explicit takeover establishes an\n1745|unambiguous checkpoint. Losing-lease branches remain preserved but are never\n1746|applied to authoritative state.\n1747|\n1748|The v1 event types are:\n1749|\n1750|<code>session.created</code>, <code>terminal.created</code>,\n1751|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>provider.identified</code>,\n1752|<code>session.idle</code>, <code>session.quiescing</code>,\n1753|<code>checkpoint.created</code>, <code>sync.completed</code>,\n1754|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1755|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1756|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1757|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1758|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1759|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1760|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1761|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1762|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1763|\n1764|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1765|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1766|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1767|\n1768|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1769|| --- | --- |\n1770|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1771|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1772|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1773|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1774|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1775|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1776|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1777|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1778|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1779|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1780|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1781|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1782|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1783|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1784|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1785|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1786|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1787|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1788|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1789|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1790|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1791|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1792|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1793|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1794|\n1795|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1796|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1797|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1798|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1799|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1800|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1801|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1802|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1803|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1804|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1805|null.\n1806|\n1807|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1808|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1809|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1810|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1811|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1812|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1813|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1814|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1815|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1816|\n1817|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1818|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1819|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1820|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1821|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1822|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1823|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1824|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1825|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1826|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1827|\n1828|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1829|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1830|\n1831|Normative example:\n1832|\n1833|~~~json\n1834|{\n1835|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1836|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1837|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1838|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1839|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1840|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1841|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1842|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1843|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1844|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1845|  \"predecessors\": [\n1846|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1847|  ],\n1848|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1849|  \"payload\": {\n1850|    \"graceful\": true,\n1851|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1852|    \"resumable\": true,\n1853|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1854|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1855|    \"store_closed\": true\n1856|  },\n1857|  \"extensions\": {}\n1858|}\n1859|~~~\n1860|\n1861|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1862|\n1863|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1864|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1865|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1866|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1867|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1868|\n1869|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1870|| --- | --- |\n1871|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1872|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1873|\n1874|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1875|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1876|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1877|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1878|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1879|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1880|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1881|\n1882|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1883|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1884|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1885|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1886|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1887|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1888|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1889|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1890|version replacement.\n1891|\n1892|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1893|\n1894|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1895|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1896|\n1897|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1898|| --- | --- | --- |\n1899|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1900|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1901|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1902|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1903|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1904|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n1905|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n1906|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n1907|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n1908|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n1909|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n1910|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n1911|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n1912|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1913|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1914|\n1915|The object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\n1916|Normative example:\n1917|\n1918|~~~json\n1919|{\n1920|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:lease\",\n1921|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1922|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:8ead987abed8c7c05175b447c9a0e2b3a521f12e5a989acb8abe132576852d63\",\n1923|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1924|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1925|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1926|  \"epoch\": 4,\n1927|  \"holder_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1928|  \"predecessor_lease_id\": \"bbbbbbbb-cccc-4ddd-8eee-ffffffffffff\",\n1929|  \"reason\": \"graceful_takeover\",\n1930|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1931|  \"issued_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1932|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1933|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:00.000Z\",\n1934|  \"extensions\": {}\n1935|}\n1936|~~~\n1937|\n1938|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n1939|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n1940|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n1941|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n1942|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n1943|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n1944|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n1945|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n1946|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n1947|\n1948|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n1949|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n1950|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n1951|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n1952|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n1953|\n1954|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
