{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b9e-4019-7d82-8599-f430d1ae00b2"},"sequence":190,"recorded_at":1780531400000375,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"97520bbe-292b-4ca0-a95c-0ff652856e64"},"task_id":"97520bbe-292b-4ca0-a95c-0ff652856e64","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"97520bbe-292b-4ca0-a95c-0ff652856e64","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(576 line(s) above)\n577|### 2.3 Session name resolution\n578|\n579|<code>ax NAME</code> MUST resolve in this order:\n580|\n581|1. exact live session name in the local derived index;\n582|2. exact live session name learned from allowlisted peers;\n583|3. exact UUID when NAME is a UUID; then\n584|4. not found.\n585|\n586|Ambiguous or case-fold-colliding names MUST fail with\n587|<code>name_ambiguous</code>. Names are displayed with original case, but\n588|uniqueness MUST use Unicode-independent ASCII case folding because the allowed\n589|alphabet is ASCII.\n590|\n591|When exactly one route is safe, non-mutating, and applicable,\n592|<code>ax NAME</code> MAY auto-attach to the current owner or resume the stopped\n593|current owner after validating its lease and execution-realm readiness. It MUST\n594|NOT rank a mutating route into an implicit action. When the owner is remote and\n595|more than the uniquely safe remote-attach route is requested, interactive mode\n596|MUST present a pure plan and offer exactly:\n597|\n598|1. remote attach;\n599|2. graceful takeover here;\n600|3. fork here; or\n601|4. cancel.\n602|\n603|Force takeover MUST NOT appear as the default choice. It is exposed by the\n604|explicit <code>ax takeover NAME --to HOST --force</code> command. Non-interactive\n605|commands MUST select the same actions explicitly; they MUST NOT prompt or infer\n606|one. Takeover, fork, move, and ambiguity return\n607|<code>interactive_choice_required</code> unless an exact plan and confirmation\n608|or equivalent explicit action flags are supplied.\n609|\n610|### 2.4 Execution profiles\n611|\n612|The persisted profile enum is <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code>.\n613|<code>yolo</code> means the provider-specific unrestricted/no-approval mode; it\n614|does not mean that <code>ax</code> ignores its own ownership, conflict,\n615|allowlist, or integrity checks.\n616|\n617|The immutable Session Record stores the creation profile. Every\n618|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n619|<code>session.resumed</code>, and <code>fork.created</code> event repeats the\n620|effective ax profile and the digest of the authoritative\n621|<code>profile.changed</code> event from which it was derived, or null when the\n622|Session Record is still the authority. A profile change requires\n623|<code>ax session set-profile NAME PROFILE</code>, a new event under the current\n624|lease, and operator confirmation when changing to <code>yolo</code>. A resume\n625|MUST fail with <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code> if the adapter cannot\n626|map the stored profile for the probed provider version.\n627|\n628|The effective persisted profile is the Session Record value followed by the\n629|newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in lease/sequence order.\n630|Losing-lease or ambiguous events MUST NOT change it. Every command that says\n631|“persisted profile” refers to this derived value. The profile source is null\n632|when no authoritative change exists and otherwise is exactly that newest\n633|event's <code>event_id</code>. A Checkpoint's event-head closure fixes both\n634|values for that checkpoint; a bundle, resume, or fork MUST NOT fall back to the\n635|Session Record creation value when the closure contains a later change.\n636|\n637|Fork creates a new authority boundary. Its new Session Record stores the\n638|source-checkpoint effective profile as its creation profile, so the new\n639|session's <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null. The\n640|<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code> separately preserves the\n641|nullable source-session event used for that projection; it is provenance and\n642|MUST NOT be treated as a profile event in the new session's event chain.\n643|\n644|Provider mapping is evidence, not profile authority. In particular, Pi 0.73.1\n645|maps both ax profiles to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code>; the two ax\n646|profiles remain distinct because the Session/Event authority and confirmation\n647|history remain distinct even when the provider mapping strings are equal.\n648|\n649|The following end-to-end profile fixtures are normative. Let P0 be the Session\n650|Record profile, E1 an authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event to P1,\n651|and C1 a checkpoint whose event-head closure contains E1:\n652|\n653|| Fixture | Path | Required profile authority |\n654|| --- | --- | --- |\n655|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER</code> | Direct start P0 → E1 → C1 → graceful/force takeover | Bundle is absent; materialization finalize, plugin resume, and resumed event all carry P1/E1 |\n656|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME</code> | Direct stop at C1 → owner resume | Plugin resume and resumed event carry P1/E1; creation P0 is ignored |\n657|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-FORK</code> | Fork C1 | New Session Record creation profile is P1; fork event carries P1/null as new-session authority plus <code>source_profile_event_id=E1</code>; resumed carries P1/null |\n658|| <code>PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER</code> | Task-board start P0 → E1 → export C1 → takeover | Bundle projection carries P1/E1; journaled bridge resume and events use the same pair |\n659|| <code>PROFILE-TB-RESUME</code> | Task-board owner resume from C1 | Bundle, bridge resume, and events agree on P1/E1 |\n660|| <code>PROFILE-TB-FORK</code> | Task-board fork C1 | Source bundle carries P1/E1; new Session Record and bridge resume use P1/null; fork event retains E1 only in <code>source_profile_event_id</code> |\n661|| <code>PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING</code> | Pi changes <code>standard</code> to <code>yolo</code> at E1 while both map to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code> | Ax still persists and reports P1/E1; equal provider argv text is not authority to erase E1 |\n662|\n663|Any fixture that uses P0 after C1, omits E1 where the event schema requires its\n664|source, or accepts a bundle profile inconsistent with C1 is\n665|<code>integrity_failure</code> before activation.\n666|\n667|## 3. Architecture and durable local layout\n668|\n669|### 3.1 Required components\n670|\n671|The implementation is logically divided into:\n672|\n673|- <strong>CLI/controller</strong>: parses commands, enforces policy, and\n674|  coordinates transactions;\n675|- <strong>state engine</strong>: validates immutable objects and derives current\n676|  state into SQLite;\n677|- <strong>terminal backend</strong>: tmux/PTTY on Unix-family systems or\n678|  process/ConPTY on native Windows;\n679|- <strong>macOS Aqua terminal broker</strong>: a minimal per-user GUI-realm\n680|  process that alone may create or attest credential-dependent tmux servers;\n681|  it is distinct from the background control plane;\n682|- <strong>provider host</strong>: discovers and invokes built-in or executable\n683|  provider adapters;\n684|- <strong>workspace engine</strong>: captures, transfers, compares, stages, and\n685|  materializes Git and non-Git state;\n686|- <strong>mesh RPC</strong>: performs SSH stdio capability negotiation and\n687|  anti-entropy exchange;\n688|- <strong>task-board bridge</strong>: treats manager bundles as opaque bytes\n689|  plus a public manifest;\n690|- <strong>derived index</strong>: local SQLite cache rebuilt from immutable\n691|  truth; and\n692|- <strong>user service</strong>: optional periodic health, reconciliation, and\n693|  sync driver;\n694|- <strong>Directory Controller</strong>: enforces discovery, disclosure,\n695|  enrichment, query, and continuation policy without acquiring a second lease\n696|  or workspace authority;\n(more lines below)"}}}
