{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c519","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b9e-4019-7d82-8599-f430d1ae00b2"},"sequence":231,"recorded_at":1780531400000457,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"868a1309-d750-4b15-8a10-0ca2d4130887"},"call_id":"call_01a07b9eca7172409fdf3455f7072748","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(10736 line(s) above)\n10737|### 14.4 List and status fields\n10738|\n10739|Text and JSON list/status MUST expose:\n10740|\n10741|- session ID and name;\n10742|- direct/task-board kind and provider;\n10743|- winning owner host/name, lease epoch, and abbreviated lease ID;\n10744|- local role <code>owner</code> or <code>replica</code>;\n10745|- derived state;\n10746|- newest validated checkpoint and age;\n10747|- workspace materialization status/conflict;\n10748|- provider/platform capability statuses;\n10749|- last successful sync per peer; and\n10750|- warnings such as stale process, conditional capability, missing\n10751|  authentication, or divergent history.\n10752|\n10753|No command MAY display or log credential values, raw transcript text, or opaque\n10754|bundle contents by default.\n10755|\n10756|### 14.5 Session Directory CLI Result 3, query, and TUI\n10757|\n10758|The merged human namespace is <code>ax sessions</code> with exact human-oriented leaves\n10759|<code>list</code>, <code>inspect</code>, <code>lineage</code>,\n10760|<code>scan</code>, <code>enrich</code>, <code>jobs</code>,\n10761|<code>plan</code>, <code>continue</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n10762|<code>attach</code>, and <code>doctor</code>, plus exact agent-oriented leaves\n10763|<code>q</code>, <code>grep</code>, and <code>m</code>. Existing <code>ax list</code>,\n10764|<code>ax status</code>, and <code>ax session clone</code> retain their v0.3\n10765|managed/clone semantics. The directory does not widen those older result types.\n10766|\n10767|CLI Result 3.0.0 retains the common top-level success envelope and defines a\n10768|closed <code>command</code> registry <code>sessions.list</code>,\n10769|<code>sessions.inspect</code>, <code>sessions.lineage</code>,\n10770|<code>sessions.scan</code>, <code>sessions.enrich</code>,\n10771|<code>sessions.jobs</code>, <code>sessions.plan</code>,\n10772|<code>sessions.continue</code>, <code>sessions.operation</code>,\n10773|<code>sessions.attach</code>, <code>sessions.doctor</code>,\n10774|<code>sessions.query</code>, <code>sessions.grep</code>, and\n10775|<code>sessions.mutate</code>. Its body is the matching one of:\n10776|\n10777|| Result tag | Exact body members |\n10778|| --- | --- |\n10779|| <code>directory_entries</code> | <code>entries:DirectoryEntry[0..1000]</code>, <code>next_cursor:string[1..1024]|null</code>, <code>partial:boolean</code>, <code>freshness:DirectoryFreshness</code> |\n10780|| <code>directory_inspection</code> | <code>entry:DirectoryEntry</code>, <code>observations:NativeSessionObservation[0..256]</code>, <code>annotations:SessionAnnotation[0..1024]</code>, <code>provenance_ids:sorted unique digest[0..4096]</code> |\n10781|| <code>directory_lineage</code> | <code>anchor_id:UUIDv7|digest</code>, <code>nodes:LineageNode[1..4096]</code>, <code>authoritative_links:ConversationLineageLink[0..4096]</code>, <code>suggestions:SuggestedRelation[0..4096]</code>, <code>ambiguous:boolean</code> |\n10782|| <code>directory_hosts_environments</code> | <code>hosts:DirectoryHost[0..1024]</code>, <code>environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..4096]</code> |\n10783|| <code>directory_jobs</code> | <code>requests:EnrichmentJobRequest[0..1000]</code>, <code>receipts:EnrichmentJobReceipt[0..4096]</code>, <code>next_cursor:string[1..1024]|null</code> |\n10784|| <code>directory_plan</code> | <code>plan:ContinuationPlan</code>, <code>outcome=planned_only</code>, <code>mutated=false</code> |\n10785|| <code>directory_operation</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>receipt_chain:DirectoryOperationReceipt[1..4096]</code>, <code>current_state:validating|executing|finalizing|succeeded|failed|uncertain|compensated</code>, <code>outcome:directory-outcome|null</code> |\n10786|| <code>directory_attach_continue</code> | <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>outcome:directory-outcome</code>, <code>target_session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>runtime_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>, <code>current_receipt_id:digest</code> |\n10787|| <code>directory_doctor</code> | <code>healthy:boolean</code>, <code>findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096]</code>, <code>contract_versions:ContractAssertion[1..64]</code>, <code>tuple_evidence_age_seconds:uint53|null</code> |\n10788|| <code>directory_query</code> | <code>query_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>results:QueryResult[1..64]</code> |\n10789|| <code>annotation_mutation</code> | <code>annotation:SessionAnnotation|null</code>, <code>would_write:boolean</code>, <code>extensions</code>; annotation is null exactly for dry run |\n10790|| <code>enrichment_mutation</code> | <code>request:EnrichmentJobRequest</code>, <code>would_enqueue:boolean</code>, <code>extensions</code> |\n10791|\n10792|Every body is closed and uses the Section 10.8 types; <code>DirectoryEntry</code>\n10793|is a result projection, not a new record. CLI Result 1 SessionSummary and CLI\n10794|Result 2 clone bodies do not acquire directory fields. Failures use Structured\n10795|Error 1.2, never <code>ok=false</code> success objects.\n10796|\n10797|The command/result mapping is exact: <code>sessions.list</code> and\n10798|<code>sessions.grep</code> use <code>directory_entries</code>;\n10799|<code>sessions.inspect</code> uses <code>directory_inspection</code>;\n10800|<code>sessions.lineage</code> uses <code>directory_lineage</code>;\n10801|<code>sessions.scan</code> uses <code>directory_hosts_environments</code>;\n10802|<code>sessions.enrich</code> and <code>sessions.jobs</code> use\n10803|<code>directory_jobs</code>; <code>sessions.plan</code> uses\n10804|<code>directory_plan</code>; <code>sessions.continue</code> and\n10805|<code>sessions.operation</code> use <code>directory_operation</code>;\n10806|<code>sessions.attach</code> uses <code>directory_attach_continue</code>;\n10807|<code>sessions.doctor</code> uses <code>directory_doctor</code>;\n10808|<code>sessions.query</code> uses <code>directory_query</code>; and\n10809|<code>sessions.mutate</code> accepts exactly one mutation Query operation and\n10810|uses <code>annotation_mutation</code> for <code>set_title</code>,\n10811|<code>set_tags</code>, and <code>set_pin</code>,\n10812|<code>enrichment_mutation</code> for <code>enrich</code>,\n10813|<code>directory_plan</code> for <code>plan_continue</code>, and\n10814|<code>directory_operation</code> for <code>execute_plan</code>. Any other\n10815|command/body pairing is invalid. <code>sessions.query</code> accepts only read\n10816|operations; a mixed read/mutation batch is rejected rather than obscuring the\n10817|top-level mutation identity.\n10818|\n10819|CLI Result 3 top-level IDs follow this closed oracle. A value described as an\n10820|AX subject is non-null exactly when that subject kind is\n10821|<code>ax_session</code>; native-instance and lineage subjects use null. A\n10822|server-assigned operation ID is stable under replay of the same idempotency\n10823|key.\n10824|\n10825|| Command tag | Top-level <code>operation_id</code> | Top-level <code>session_id</code> |\n10826|| --- | --- | --- |\n10827|| <code>sessions.list</code> | null | null |\n10828|| <code>sessions.inspect</code> | null | inspected AX subject, else null |\n10829|| <code>sessions.lineage</code> | null | null; an AX-shaped anchor is not a Session ID assertion |\n10830|| <code>sessions.scan</code> | non-null server-assigned scan operation | null |\n10831|| <code>sessions.enrich</code> | non-null server-assigned enqueue operation | enriched AX subject, else null |\n10832|| <code>sessions.jobs</code> | null | null |\n10833|| <code>sessions.plan</code> | null because planning is pure | plan source Session ID, else null |\n10834|| <code>sessions.continue</code> | non-null and equal the body/receipt-chain operation | plan source Session ID, else null |\n10835|| <code>sessions.operation</code> | non-null and equal the queried body/receipt-chain operation | validated source Session ID, else null |\n10836|| <code>sessions.attach</code> | non-null and equal the body operation | body <code>target_session_id</code> when non-null, otherwise plan source Session ID or null |\n10837|| <code>sessions.doctor</code> | null | null |\n10838|| <code>sessions.query</code> | null | null |\n10839|| <code>sessions.grep</code> | null | null; grep's source-local physical scope is carried in its request |\n10840|| <code>sessions.mutate</code> | null for every dry run and for pure <code>plan_continue</code>; non-null server-assigned for confirmed annotation/enrichment mutation; for <code>execute_plan</code>, non-null and equal its parameter/body operation | mutation AX subject, or the executed plan's source Session ID; otherwise null |\n10841|\n10842|For <code>annotation_mutation</code>, dry run requires null annotation,\n10843|<code>would_write=true|false</code> as the authorization/expectation preview,\n10844|and null top-level operation ID; confirmed mutation requires a non-null newly\n10845|published or idempotently replayed annotation, <code>would_write=false</code>,\n10846|and non-null operation ID. For <code>enrichment_mutation</code>, dry run has\n10847|<code>would_enqueue=true|false</code> and null top-level operation ID;\n10848|confirmation has <code>would_enqueue=false</code>, a request that was newly\n10849|enqueued or recovered by idempotency key, and a non-null operation ID.\n10850|<code>plan_continue</code> is always a dry-run mutation operation and retains\n10851|null operation ID. <code>execute_plan</code> is never dry-run and uses its\n10852|explicit UUIDv7 throughout.\n10853|\n10854|The <code>sessions.continue</code> partial-success outcome\n10855|<code>cloned_source_still_active</code> does not switch the top-level Session\n10856|ID to the new target: it remains the source Session ID under the table, while\n10857|the valid target identity stays in the receipt chain and durable effects. This\n10858|prevents a partial move from presenting the source-release failure as a\n10859|different operation or authority.\n10860|\n10861|The agent surface is <code>ax sessions q</code>,\n10862|<code>ax sessions grep</code>, and <code>ax sessions m</code>, all using\n10863|Directory Query Schema 1. Query supports field projection, batches up to 64,\n10864|bounded <code>skip</code>/<code>take</code>, deterministic sorting, schema\n10865|discovery, and typed filters. Mutations use the exact dry-run/confirmation/\n10866|expectation semantics in Section 10.8. There is no delete. Agents MUST NOT\n10867|scrape terminal/TUI text.\n10868|\n10869|Default list/query output may include sanitized resolved title, summary, recent\n10870|activity, open loops, freshness, reachability, and conflicts, but no raw\n10871|excerpt. Explicit preview/transcript grep names one source host and instance,\n10872|is redacted and bounded, and cannot fan out. Machine clients branch on result\n10873|tag, structured error code, and receipt state rather than messages or process\n10874|exit alone.\n10875|\n10876|The Session Browser TUI is another client of the same engine. It has four\n10877|bounded regions: filter/status bar; lineage/session table; detail/preview/\n10878|provenance pane; and semantic action/help bar. The default row is Conversation\n10879|Lineage. Expansion shows AX Sessions and native instances. Selection survives\n10880|refresh by stable ID, never row number.\n10881|\n10882|Minimum keys are <code>j/k</code> or arrows, <code>Enter</code>,\n10883|<code>/</code> search, <code>f</code> filter, <code>s</code> sort,\n10884|<code>r</code> refresh, <code>e</code> enrich, <code>c</code> plan,\n10885|<code>a</code> attach, <code>o</code> open/resume, <code>J</code> jobs/\n10886|receipts, <code>?</code> help, and <code>q</code> leave. Navigation, filtering,\n10887|preview-mode changes, and plan inspection are read-only. Every mutation calls\n10888|the same planner/executor; no TUI-only path exists. Disabled actions remain\n10889|visible with structured reasons.\n10890|\n10891|The continuation wizard selects semantic intent, exact source instance, target\n10892|host, exact installed Environment Tuple, workspace/cohort policy, fidelity and\n10893|source-after-success policy, then displays every plan expectation/effect/\n10894|confirmation before execution. Offline/stale/conflicted rows remain visible.\n10895|Narrow layouts drop prose before identity, owner, freshness, or warnings.\n10896|Provider/transcript strings are rendered as data: ANSI, OSC, bidi overrides,\n10897|controls, invalid width, and hostile grapheme sequences are removed or visibly\n10898|escaped. Terminal transport, resize, reconnect, and process supervision remain\n10899|Section 4 authority.\n10900|\n10901|### 14.6 CLI Result 4.0.0 TerminalBackend surfaces\n10902|\n10903|CLI Result 4.0.0 retains the exact CLI Result 3 top-level success envelope,\n10904|every v1-v3 command/result body not named below, and their top-level ID rules.\n10905|It adds the closed command tags <code>terminal.backend.list</code>,\n10906|<code>terminal.backend.show</code>, <code>terminal.backend.probe</code>, and\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
